    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.74) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.10) anchoring the lineup, both benefiting from highly favorable platoon splits and strong expected run-production environments. **Josh Jung** (68.56) is a standout play for today; despite the \"Lineup Pending\" tag, his favorable matchup against the soft-tossing Quintana, combined with a significant park factor boost, makes him a premier asset. While **Kyle Tucker** (65.32) remains a stable cornerstone, the team\u2019s offensive ceiling is heavily tied to the performances of **Guerrero Jr.** and **Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose ability to capitalize on their respective RHP matchups is vital given our strategic focus on maintaining efficiency across all five categories.\n\nWe have opted to bench **Nolan Schanuel** (52.69) in favor of the current starters, as he finished as our highest-ranked omission. While **Schanuel** possesses a solid projection, he was nudged out by **Drake Baldwin** and **Andy Pages** due to the latter\u2019s specific situational advantages. **Gunnar Henderson** (49.79) remains in the lineup despite a sub-50 efficiency score; although he faces a tough southpaw in McClanahan, his elite speed and the 2% boost gained from the pitcher's slow delivery make him a necessary gamble to secure stolen bases, our scarcest category. Managers should monitor **Josh Jung**\u2019s confirmed spot in the order, as a move down from the assumed #3 slot would warrant a re-evaluation of his current daily efficiency score.",
